# C2-S04 / S06 / S07 and the Ironhold ambient + camp conversations.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 2206–2306, 2719–2848.
# Scene: scenes/regions/ironhold_region.tscn. One node per NPC; the
# dispatcher nodes pick a line by story state, so each visit says something new.
# Source fix: the old "Engineer Mira" is gone (Mira Chen is Kaelen's Earth
# contact), and Seraphina no longer lectures about Root Access before meeting him.
# rhythm: clipped convoy
# (Seraphina counting heads under pressure. The short lines are the point.)

# ── Rook (market) — C2-S07 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

~ rook
[if not ch2_rook_met] => rook_first
[if not ch2_market_visited] => rook_market
=> rook_repeat

~ rook_first
set ch2_rook_met
Rook: You're the one the Commander walked through the gate. People are already guessing what you cost her.
Kaelen: Cost her? Cost her what?
Rook: Credibility, mostly. Rook. I move things from where they're cheap to where they aren't.
=> rook_market

~ rook_market
set ch2_market_visited
Rook: First rule. Buy low.
Kaelen: Sell high. Everyone knows that one.
Rook: You've got markets where you come from.
Kaelen: Unfortunately. Big ones, with screens.
Rook: Then you know the real first rule.
Kaelen: There's always a fee. Somebody always takes a cut.
# He smiles like he didn't mean to.
Rook: I might like you. Don't let it go to your head.
Rook: Prices here move with the roads, the season, and who's been nice to whom. The auction board's over there if you want to lose money slowly. Nobody makes you bid.
[if ch2_medicine_quest_active and not ch2_medicine_done] Rook: And don't buy healing resin today. If that convoy's late, whoever's holding resin gets rich off sick people. This city remembers who did that.

~ rook_repeat
[if not ch2_medicine_done] Rook: Resin's still climbing. Somebody's praying that convoy's late.
[if ch2_medicine_done] Rook: Convoy came in, resin dropped, and three men I can't stand lost a fortune. Best day I've had all month.

# ── The street — C2-S04 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

~ preacher
[if ch2_administrator_proxy_defeated] => preacher_after_proxy
Preacher: The tower counts our sins! Every stroke of that bell, another one written down!
Citizen: It counts minutes. That's all it's ever counted.
Preacher: Same thing, if you're late enough.

~ preacher_after_proxy
Citizen: They say the Proxy kept crime down, while it was running.
Citizen: It kept people down. That's not the same thing.
Preacher: Then what was it counting all those years?

~ garro
Garro: Root Access can't sharpen steel. Whatever else it does.
Kaelen: I didn't say it could. I haven't said anything.
Garro: Good. I've got enough competition.

~ sol
Sol: Lot twelve! One compass, from before the Fracture!
Kaelen: Does it actually work?
Sol: It points somewhere. That's more than most of us can say.

~ dice
Dice Host: Dice? Three silver a throw. House is honest. Mostly.
Elara: No.
Kaelen: I didn't say anything.
Elara: Your face did. Your face said a great deal.

~ doss
[if ch2_medicine_done] Doss: Resin! Cheap! Cheaper than this morning, I swear! Please!
[if not ch2_medicine_done] Doss: Healing resin, last few jars! Price goes up every hour that convoy's out, so buy now!

~ paladins
[if ch2_data_wraith_restored] => paladins_restored
[if ch2_data_wraith_destroyed] => paladins_destroyed
Paladin: The Commander slept. I saw it with my own eyes.
Nori: Prove it.
Paladin: Her eyes were closed. For ages.
Seraphina: I blinked.
[if ch2_underground_unlocked] Nori: Lower streets are sealed past the market stairs. If you're going down, don't go down alone.

~ paladins_restored
Worker: Iven woke up this morning. First time in years.
Nori: Which Iven? We've got three.
Worker: That's the problem. He doesn't know either.

~ paladins_destroyed
Rem: The tunnels are quiet now. Nothing moving down there.
Rem: I thought quiet would feel better than this.

# ── Healer Rem and the medicine convoy — C2-S06 (time-sensitive) ──────────
# Deadline: the evening bell. In this build the bell is the Clock Tower
# stopping (clock_tower.dlg "bell"), which happens when the player goes up the
# tower. Early = before the arena's bronze bracket is won; on time = before the bell;
# late = after it (the region sets ch2_medicine_early / _on_time / _late).

~ rem
[if ch2_medicine_done] => rem_after
[if ch2_medicine_quest_active] => rem_waiting
Rem: You're the Commander's outsider. Good. I need somebody who isn't on a duty roster.
Rem: There's fever in the lower city. The medicine's on a convoy out west, stuck behind a fractured road.
Kaelen: How long have you got?
Rem: Until the evening bell. After that the gates close, and the fever does what it likes.
? Kaelen (Internal): The convoy.
- I'll go now. => rem_go_now
- I'll get there. Soon. => rem_later

~ rem_go_now
set ch2_medicine_quest_active
do quest_start medicine_convoy
Rem: West road. Take the Commander if she'll come. She always comes.

~ rem_later
set ch2_medicine_quest_active
do quest_start medicine_convoy
Rem: "Soon" is a word I hear a lot in here. West road. Before the bell.

~ rem_waiting
Rem: Evening bell. West road. I'm not going to keep saying it nicely.

~ rem_after
[if ch2_medicine_early] Rem: You got it here early. If this city does something stupid tonight, I'll have beds to spare.
[if ch2_medicine_on_time] Rem: In time. That's all I ask of anyone, and hardly anyone manages it.
[if ch2_medicine_late] Rem: It came. After the bell. Tomas and the Wren girl are still burning up. Don't apologise to me. Apologise to them when they can hear you.
Kaelen: What do you call those blue potions?
Rem: Breath. Because that's what they give back.
Kaelen: That's a better name than ours.

# The escort, on the west road (region story gate). Seraphina counts.
~ convoy
do fade_to_road
Seraphina: Forty-two.
Kaelen: You keep counting.
Seraphina: Forty-two people. Six wagons.
Kaelen: People first.
Seraphina: People first. Wagons second.
Kaelen: You did that on the plane.
Seraphina: Don't.
Kaelen: Sorry.
# She nods. She doesn't stop counting.
do convoy_ambush
Seraphina: Forty-two. All of them.
[if ch2_seraphina_truth] => convoy_count
=> convoy_done

~ convoy_count
Seraphina: I counted then, too. On the plane. Afterwards.
Seraphina: I stopped at one hundred and eighty-six.
# Kaelen says nothing. It's the right thing to say.
Seraphina: There were more.
set ch2_seraphina_186_told
=> convoy_done

~ convoy_done
set ch2_medicine_done
do trust seraphina 10

# ── Seraphina off duty (city NPC) and the camp conversations ──────────────

~ seraphina
[if not ch2_ks_01_done] => ks_01
[if not ch2_es_01_done] => es_01
[if ch2_medicine_done and not ch2_ks_02_done] => ks_02
[if ch2_arena_bronze_complete and not ch2_es_02_done] => es_02
[if ch2_clock_tower_complete and not ch2_ks_03_done] => ks_03
[if ch2_clock_tower_complete and not ch2_es_03_done] => es_03
=> seraphina_idle

~ ks_01
set ch2_ks_01_done
Kaelen: Do you remember the impact? The actual moment?
Seraphina: Yes. Every part of it.
Kaelen: I don't. There's just a gap.
Seraphina: Don't be jealous.

~ ks_02
set ch2_ks_02_done
Seraphina: You had coffee.
Kaelen: On the plane?
Seraphina: Before boarding. You spilled it down your sleeve.
Kaelen: That's a weirdly specific thing to remember.
Seraphina: I spent the first hour of the flight trying not to look at the stain.

~ ks_03
set ch2_ks_03_done
Kaelen: Why a paladin? Of everything you could've been here.
Seraphina: The armour was available.
Kaelen: That's it? That's the whole reason?
Seraphina: At first. Then people started listening to me.
Kaelen: Why did they listen?
Seraphina: Because I knew what to do when people were frightened. It turns out panic sounds the same under any sky.

~ es_01
set ch2_es_01_done
Seraphina: Your arm's getting worse.
Elara: Everyone's so observant lately.
Seraphina: I was trained.
Elara: To watch arms? That's a strange thing to train for.
Seraphina: To watch people pretending they're fine.
# Elara looks away.
Elara: That's dangerous training.

~ es_02
set ch2_es_02_done
Elara: Flight attendant. That's what he called you.
Seraphina: Yes.
Elara: You served food. In the sky.
Seraphina: Among other things.
Elara: And then you became Knight-Commander.
Seraphina: Career change.
Elara: That isn't a career change. I don't think there's a word for what that is.

~ es_03
set ch2_es_03_done
Seraphina: Is he always like this?
Elara: Kaelen? Like what, exactly?
Seraphina: Who else?
Elara: He's worse when he's scared. Much worse.
Kaelen: I can hear you, you know.
Elara: See? That's the scared voice.

~ seraphina_idle
[if ch2_administrator_proxy_defeated] Seraphina: Brask wants a report on the Proxy. I've written "it was running the city" three times. He keeps sending it back.
[if not ch2_administrator_proxy_defeated] Seraphina: If you're looking for trouble, the market has it cheaper. If you're looking for me, I'm here until the next bell.

~ ina
Ina: Knight-Commander!
Seraphina: Off duty, Ina.
Ina: But are you still a knight when you're off duty?
Seraphina: Unfortunately. It doesn't come off with the armour.

~ vex
Vex: Arena's open! Bring your teeth, take home fewer!

# Before the Clock Tower: the convoy's deadline is the bell (fair warning).
~ tower_warning
Seraphina: The convoy's still out on the west road. When that tower rings again, the gates close behind it.
? Kaelen (Internal): Go up anyway?
- Not yet. The convoy first. => END
- We go up now. => tower_go

~ tower_go
set ch2_tower_go_now
